  "content": {
    "id": "p31-q61-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "61",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following expressions.\n$$\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{3x+10}{(x+1)(x+2)}$, $x\\ne-1,-2$.\n\nFactorise the quadratic denominator and use a common denominator.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}&=\\frac4{(x+1)(x+2)}+\\frac{3(x+2)}{(x+1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}&=\\frac{4+3x+6}{(x+1)(x+2)}\\\\\\frac4{x^2+3x+2}+\\frac3{x+1}&=\\frac{3x+10}{(x+1)(x+2)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe original denominators require $x\\ne-1,-2$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
  },
